WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.740
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.290
And boy, we left this poor lady

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.140
whose children had died,
whose parents had died,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.940
whose husbands had died,

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.700
who had been buried alive a few times.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.330
And we left her. She finally
came to where the Buddha was.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.070
And something strange happens.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:26.410
The Buddha stands up far away.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.350
I guess it's in the Garden
of Jetavana, in Shravasti

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.720
where he taught the Diamond Cutter.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.690
He looks on her and he says, "Welcome".

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.950
It's supposed to be very strange

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.540
that the Buddha would stand up

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.170
for someone else who walks in
the room and says, "Welcome."

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.865
And he says, "Come to me."

00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:50.017
Then she's embarrassed to stand up

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:51.373
because she doesn't have any clothes on,

00:00:51.373 --> 00:00:56.373
because she was just dug
out of a grave by a wolf/

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.595
So here we go.

00:01:00.595 --> 00:01:01.728
DE NAS BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.044
KUN DGA' BO LA BKA' STZAL PA

00:01:04.044 --> 00:01:06.128
Then the Buddha said to

00:01:06.128 --> 00:01:08.594
KUN DGA' BO Who is that?

00:01:08.594 --> 00:01:11.093
[Student] Ananda. [GMR] Ananda, yay!

00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:13.353
BUD MED 'DI LA GOS SKON CIG

00:01:13.353 --> 00:01:16.850
means get some clothes on this lady.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.272
Give this lady come clothes.

00:01:18.272 --> 00:01:20.607
SKON CIG CES BKA' STZAL PA

00:01:20.607 --> 00:01:22.332
BKA' STZAL PA is a very high, high, high

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:26.268
honorific word for he bespoke.

00:01:26.268 --> 00:01:28.420
KHO MOS GOS GYON NAS

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.947
Then she's telling the story.

00:01:29.947 --> 00:01:34.400
KHO MO means me, feminine,
ancient, ancient, ancient.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.576
So this sutra is very old.

00:01:35.576 --> 00:01:38.818
KHO MOS GOS GYON NAS

00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:40.161
I put the clothes on.

00:01:40.161 --> 00:01:42.900
BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYI ZHABS
LA MGO BOS PHYAG 'TSAL TE

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.840
I did a prostration to Lord Buddha

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.340
and touched my head to his feet.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.098
BDAG LA THUGS BRTZE BAR DGONGS NAS

00:01:50.098 --> 00:01:53.140
Please love me. Please show me your love.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.580
BDAG RAB TU 'BYUNG BAR GNOD

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.180
Please ordain me.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.970
Please grant me the vows of a nun.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:06.970
And this GNOD, usually it means
to hurt somebody, G-N-O-D.

00:02:08.778 --> 00:02:12.038
But here it's the imperative of NOD PA

00:02:12.038 --> 00:02:16.720
which means to grant vows.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.750
So you won't see it.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.140
It's one out of 10,000 something.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.847
She's not asking the Buddha to hurt her.

00:02:25.822 --> 00:02:27.897
ZHIG CES GSOL PA

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:29.563
She says, I requested Him.

00:02:29.563 --> 00:02:32.010
BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS KUS
DGA' BO LA BKA' STAL TE

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.492
Then the Buddha said to Ananda

00:02:34.492 --> 00:02:37.959
BUD MED 'DI SKYE RGU'I BDAG MO LA GTAD

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:41.384
Let's turn this woman over to

00:02:41.384 --> 00:02:43.927
SKYE RGU'I BDAG MO

00:02:43.927 --> 00:02:46.383
SKYE RGU means all the
beings of the universe.

00:02:46.383 --> 00:02:48.930
BDAG MO means the lady in charge

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.030
of all the beings in the universe.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:54.820
This is a name for Prajapati,

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:58.536
who was the Buddha's foster mother.

00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:01.100
The Buddha's own mother died

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.720
about a week after she gave birth to him.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.544
Then he spent his whole childhood

00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:10.600
being taken care of by Prajapati.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.740
Then when he became the Buddha,

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.120
she became the first nun
of all in this world.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.890
There's a picture of
her here, kind of corny.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.260
I thought, boy, this
picture's probably painted by

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.140
some crazy person in France or something.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.830
But it's actually painted in Sri Lanka.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.479
This is a painting of
Prajapati and Lord Buddha.

00:03:37.479 --> 00:03:39.890
She was his foster mother.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.890
So Buddha says, "Take this
homeless lady who just crawled

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.880
out of a grave and turn
her over to Prajapati."

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:47.713
And she can

00:03:47.713 --> 00:03:49.888
RAB TU PHYUNG ZHIG

00:03:49.888 --> 00:03:51.210
imperative tense.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.450
She can ordain this woman.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.897
It's also interesting

00:03:57.897 --> 00:04:01.840
that the Buddha is asking
a woman to ordain a woman.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.711
Nowadays, I think a guy has
to be there, right Jigme?

00:04:06.711 --> 00:04:08.870
[Ven. Jigme] Yes, certain number of guys.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.380
[GMR] Yes, but that's kind of strange.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.207
It seems like in the original
times Buddha's like saying,

00:04:13.207 --> 00:04:15.130
all the ladies can take
care of the ladies.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:20.123
I don't know, probably
changed at some point.

00:04:22.463 --> 00:04:25.906
DE NAS SKYE RGU'I BDAG MOS
KHO MO RAB TU PHYUNG NAS

00:04:25.906 --> 00:04:29.834
Then Prajapati ordained me.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.890
KHO MO LA BDEN PA BZHI'I CHOS BSTAN

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:35.443
She taught me the four higher truths.

00:04:35.443 --> 00:04:37.451
KHO MOS THOS MA THAG TU

00:04:37.451 --> 00:04:41.090
Just after I heard
about those four truths:

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.900
Everything is suffering,

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.520
There's a cause of the suffering.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.330
You can stop the suffering.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:49.489
There's a path to stop the suffering.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.275
BRTZON 'GRUS SU NAN TAN BYAS PAS

00:04:52.275 --> 00:04:55.490
I worked very hard to
practice what she taught me

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.634
about the four truths.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.133
DGRA BCOM PA THOB

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.975
What's that mean?

00:05:00.975 --> 00:05:01.808
I

00:05:01.808 --> 00:05:04.249
THOB DGRA BCOM PA

00:05:04.249 --> 00:05:07.995
I achieved DGRA BCOM PA

00:05:07.995 --> 00:05:11.526
Arhat. I became an arhat. That's so cool.

00:05:11.526 --> 00:05:14.350
To be honest, you don't see a lot

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:18.810
of stories of ladies reaching
nirvana in the ancient books

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.930
because it was such a
male dominated culture.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.566
But in this story she's the heroine.

00:05:25.566 --> 00:05:27.299
DGRA BCOM PA THOB STE

00:05:27.299 --> 00:05:29.074
I achieved arhat.

00:05:29.074 --> 00:05:30.532
'DAS PA DANG, MA 'ONGS PA DANG,

00:05:30.532 --> 00:05:32.749
DA LTAR GYI BYA BA KUN RTOGS PAR GYUR TO

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:34.460
And very importantly,

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:38.660
I gained the power to see
all the events of the past,

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.340
the future, and the present.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.570
I could see what was going on,

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:48.420
which is a segue by Lord
Buddha into the next section.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.507
What's the next section going to be then?

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.290
They're going to tell the story

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.626
of why she got buried
twice and all this stuff.

00:05:58.626 --> 00:06:00.784
DGE SLONG MA DE RNAMS KYIS SMRAS PA

00:06:00.784 --> 00:06:03.850
Remember that she has
like 500 nuns around her.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.440
She's telling a story.
She's already famous.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.150
What did they ask her to start this story?

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.820
How did this story start?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.751
The nuns came to her and
said, "We still feel,

00:06:16.751 --> 00:06:21.734
we still feel attracted to guys

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:24.884
and having a nice house.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.800
You know, we became nuns, but frankly,

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.070
we're still attracted to guys,
and we're still attracted

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.578
to having a nice house and all this stuff.

00:06:33.578 --> 00:06:37.470
SNGON LAS CI BGYIS NA

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.846
What karma did you do before that

00:06:40.846 --> 00:06:43.554
DE LTA BU'I RNAM PAR
SMIN PA MYONG BA STON CIG

00:06:43.554 --> 00:06:47.490
that you could get the karmic maturations

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.170
that you have described to us?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.100
Since you're an arhat,

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.380
you can see all the past history.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:58.490
So you can tell us why you
went through all this stuff

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:00.960
in the past before you became a nun.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.885
By the way, her motivation
is to encourage them

00:07:04.885 --> 00:07:08.676
not to be attached to family life.

00:07:08.676 --> 00:07:12.768
DGE SLONG MA AUTPA LAS
KHYED RTAG PAR NYON CIG

00:07:12.768 --> 00:07:15.005
You guys, listen up.

00:07:15.005 --> 00:07:16.948
KHYED LA BSTAN PAR BYA'O

00:07:16.948 --> 00:07:20.640
Now I'll tell you what
happened before all of this,

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.640
what was the karma that I
had to go through all that.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.706
ZHES SMRAS SO

00:07:23.706 --> 00:07:27.321
SNGON 'DAS PA'I DUS YUN RING PO ZHIG NA

00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:30.469
So long, long ago, once upon a time

00:07:30.469 --> 00:07:34.660
KHYIM BDAG SHIN TU PHYUG PA ZHIG LA

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.574
there was a very wealthy householder.

00:07:38.574 --> 00:07:40.210
BU MED PA LAS

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:44.753
He hadn't had a son yet to
carry on his family line.

00:07:44.753 --> 00:07:46.692
CHUN MA ZHIG BLANGS

00:07:46.692 --> 00:07:51.347
So he took on a junior wife

00:07:51.347 --> 00:07:54.211
CHUN MA means a second wife.

00:07:54.211 --> 00:07:57.444
Excuse me.

00:07:57.444 --> 00:07:59.260
CHUN MA DE LA SHIN TU BYAMS PAS

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.907
He had a lot of BYAMS PA to that CHUN MA.

00:08:02.907 --> 00:08:04.907
[Student] Love.

00:08:04.907 --> 00:08:09.361
Yeah, here BYAMS PA is in
the sense of worldly love.

00:08:09.361 --> 00:08:11.340
RING PO MA LON PAR CHUN MA DE

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.500
Because of that, before long,

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.038
the CHUN MA got a SEMS CAN.

00:08:18.038 --> 00:08:20.012
Yes, got pregnant, good.

00:08:20.012 --> 00:08:22.290
Remember? She got a sentient being,

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.168
meaning she got pregnant.

00:08:24.168 --> 00:08:25.770
ZLA BA TSANG NAS

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.490
When the time was right.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.636
Second paragraph.

00:08:29.636 --> 00:08:31.136
When the time was,

00:08:31.136 --> 00:08:34.621
When the required nine months had passed.

00:08:34.621 --> 00:08:36.320
KHYE'U ZHIG BTZAS TE

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.811
BTZAS means

00:08:38.811 --> 00:08:40.820
BTZAS is the Buddhist word for born

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.380
because in Buddhism the word
born refers to conception.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.930
So BTZAS means to drop out.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.160
It means come out of the womb.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.718
So we would say born.

00:08:51.718 --> 00:08:54.893
KHYO SHUG GNYIS DE LA BYAMS
SHING SDUG PAR 'DZIN TO

00:08:54.893 --> 00:08:56.643
And the husband and wife

00:08:56.643 --> 00:08:57.743
KHYO SHUG

00:08:57.743 --> 00:09:01.520
were very much in love with that boy.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.150
SDUG PAR'DZIN TO

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.290
kept him very, he looked
very attractive to them.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:11.270
This SDUG PA is the SDUG in SDUG BSNGAL,

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.910
but it means the opposite.
So this is tricky.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.370
You have to be careful
when you're translating it.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:20.368
It means they couldn't
keep their eyes off of him.

00:09:22.239 --> 00:09:25.320
DE NAS CHEN MAS 'DI SNYAM DU BSAMS SO

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:30.141
Then the older wife,
what... the first wife?

00:09:30.141 --> 00:09:32.010
[Student] She got jealous?

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:35.101
[GMR] Well, she got
jealous, right. Of course.

00:09:35.101 --> 00:09:36.711
'DI SNYAM DU BSAMS SO

00:09:36.711 --> 00:09:37.544
KHO MO NI

00:09:37.544 --> 00:09:39.085
She said to herself, I am

00:09:39.085 --> 00:09:41.670
RIGS CHE ZHING BTZUN MOD KYI

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:46.670
I am a high cast and I am a spiritual.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.460
I belong to a spiritual cast.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.599
The wanderer cast probably.

00:09:50.599 --> 00:09:53.700
BU MED PAS

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.970
By the way, this isn't BU MED

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:56.803
This is

00:09:56.803 --> 00:09:57.768
BU

00:09:57.768 --> 00:09:58.601
MED

00:09:59.838 --> 00:10:03.057
Good. BU MED means woman,
which means somebody

00:10:03.057 --> 00:10:08.057
without a certain organ,
which is a bad word,

00:10:08.382 --> 00:10:10.400
but that's the Tibetan word for woman.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.070
SKYES DMAN which means lower birth.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:16.720
The two ancient words for a woman.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.780
Probably, wo-man is similar by the way.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:24.740
And then here it means BU MED PAS

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.070
which means I don't have a son.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:28.876
Therefore, RIGS 'TSOB PA MED DO

00:10:28.876 --> 00:10:30.376
RIGS 'TSOB PA

00:10:30.376 --> 00:10:32.092
RIGS means the family line.

00:10:32.092 --> 00:10:34.808
'TSOB PA means someone to
carry on the family line.

00:10:34.808 --> 00:10:39.139
So I don't have a son to
carry on the family line.

00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:41.756
GAL TE KHYE'U 'DI CHER SKYES NA

00:10:41.756 --> 00:10:44.121
And then if this boy grows up,

00:10:44.121 --> 00:10:48.454
RIGS 'TSO BCING NOR DANG LONGS
SPYOD KYI BDAG POR 'GYUR TE

00:10:48.454 --> 00:10:51.169
he will take over the family line,

00:10:51.169 --> 00:10:53.920
and he will have lots of
money and possessions.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.140
He will take possession

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.459
of all the possessions of our family.

00:10:58.459 --> 00:10:59.392
BDAG LA MI STER

00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:01.160
And he won't give them to me.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.158
They won't give them to me.

00:11:03.158 --> 00:11:04.808
BDAG SDUG PAR 'GYUR RO

00:11:04.808 --> 00:11:07.280
Now here's SDUG PA as the opposite.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:11.670
And I will suffer.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.515
I will want.

00:11:13.515 --> 00:11:14.823
SNYAM DU PHRAG DOG SKYES

00:11:14.823 --> 00:11:16.340
She got PHRAG DOG

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.740
What's that, Tim?

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:19.879
PHRAG DOG

00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:23.458
One of the mental afflictions.

00:11:23.458 --> 00:11:25.641
She got jealous.

00:11:25.641 --> 00:11:26.474
PHRAG DOG

00:11:26.474 --> 00:11:28.556
She got very jealous.

00:11:28.556 --> 00:11:29.797
BSAD PAR BSAMS

00:11:29.797 --> 00:11:32.080
This BSAD PA means to kill.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.930
She thought, she got the
thought, I will kill this child.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.578
And then very terrible story.

00:11:38.578 --> 00:11:40.511
BU KHYE'U'I 'TSOG MAR

00:11:40.511 --> 00:11:43.440
'TSOG MAR means the top
of the skull of the child.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:47.350
She stuck a needle in the top

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.540
of the skull of the baby.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.416
KHAB means needle.

00:11:52.416 --> 00:11:55.106
BTZUGS means she stuck a
needle in the top of the...

00:11:55.106 --> 00:11:56.640
RMA YANG MI SNANG BAR BYAS SO

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.500
She did it in such a way

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:02.177
that nobody could see that
there was a hole there.

00:12:02.177 --> 00:12:05.430
So she shoved a knitting
needle into his head

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.560
and took it out slowly,

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.750
and made sure nobody could see the place

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:12.800
where she pushed in the needle.
It's terrible, terrible.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.530
I mean, cooking the child.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:15.820
Now you have to kill your child.

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:17.485
It's very weird.

00:12:17.485 --> 00:12:19.620
KHYE'U YANG RING POR MA LON PAR

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:22.503
That boy also before long

00:12:22.503 --> 00:12:23.605
TSE 'DAS PA

00:12:23.605 --> 00:12:26.833
he passed away, his life passed.

00:12:26.833 --> 00:12:28.240
CHUN MA 'KHAMS NAS

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.930
And the younger wife, what do you call it?

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.816
She fell unconscious.

00:12:34.816 --> 00:12:35.649
CHEN MA LA

00:12:35.649 --> 00:12:39.416
Then when she recovered, she said,

00:12:39.416 --> 00:12:41.990
CHEN MA LA KHYOD KYIS NGA'I BU BSAD DO

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:45.525
She said to the older wife,
I think you killed my child.

00:12:45.525 --> 00:12:47.216
ZHES BRGAL TO

00:12:47.216 --> 00:12:49.895
This BRGAL means to, sometimes

00:12:49.895 --> 00:12:53.320
BRGAL means to cross
the ocean of suffering.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:57.236
There's a famous verse in
the Bodhisattva Vow Ceremony.

00:12:57.236 --> 00:13:02.136
When we say, "I will free those
who have yet to be freed,"

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.270
this is the verb used
there to cross the ocean.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:09.230
But here it means to argue with somebody.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.800
So she BRGAL-ed to the older wife,

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.536
"I think you killed my boy."

00:13:14.536 --> 00:13:16.478
CHEN MAS BSNYON NAS

00:13:16.478 --> 00:13:21.033
means the older wife
denied the accusations.

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:23.358
'DI SKAD CES MNA' BOR

00:13:23.358 --> 00:13:25.230
MNA 'BOR means, it's ancient,

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.653
these are all ancient, ancient words.

00:13:28.653 --> 00:13:30.787
MNA' BO means to take an oath,

00:13:30.787 --> 00:13:34.795
to swear on your Bible
or to swear something.

00:13:34.795 --> 00:13:37.162
MNA' BOR RO

00:13:37.162 --> 00:13:39.700
KHO MOS KHYOD KYI BU BSAD PAR GYUR NA

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.639
If it's true that I killed your son,

00:13:42.639 --> 00:13:46.172
KHO MOS SKYE BA THAMS CAD
DU KHO MO'I KHYO SBRUL

00:13:46.172 --> 00:13:48.806
GDUG PAS BSAD PAR SHOG CIG

00:13:48.806 --> 00:13:51.080
Then in all my future lives

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:56.080
may my husbands be bitten
by poisonous snakes and die.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:59.380
She's like, "If it's true
that I hurt your son,

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.010
then in all my future
lives may all my husbands

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:05.258
get bitten by snakes and die."

00:14:07.121 --> 00:14:08.970
BU ZHIG YOD NA YANG CHUS KHYER BA

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:12.080
And if I happen to have a son,

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.993
may he be carried away by a river

00:14:17.222 --> 00:14:18.055
or

00:14:18.055 --> 00:14:19.296
SBYANG KYI ZA BAR

00:14:19.296 --> 00:14:23.240
or consumed by a wolf.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.680
SHOG CIG means may it happen.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:30.680
If it's me who killed
your son, then I vow.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:32.566
This is my vow.

00:14:32.566 --> 00:14:35.310
KHO MO'I LUS KYANG GSON POR DUR DU BCUG

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.953
And may I be buried
alive in a grave myself.

00:14:41.334 --> 00:14:43.357
BU'I SHA ZA BAR SHOG CIG

00:14:43.357 --> 00:14:46.467
And may I even eat the
flesh of my own son,

00:14:46.467 --> 00:14:49.166
if it's true that I hurt your son.

00:14:49.166 --> 00:14:52.116
PHA MA'I KHYIM DU ME SHOR TE

00:14:52.116 --> 00:14:54.983
May the home of my parents catch on fire.

00:14:54.983 --> 00:14:56.760
THAMS CAD TSIG PAR SHOG

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.533
And may everybody that
lives there be burned up.

00:14:59.533 --> 00:15:01.191
CIG SMRAS SO

00:15:01.191 --> 00:15:03.924
She swore like that.

00:15:05.301 --> 00:15:10.293
DE'I TSE NA DE SKAD CES
MNA' BOR BA'I CHEN MA DE NI

00:15:11.567 --> 00:15:15.520
"Guess who is the older
wife of those days?"

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.851
She says, you know, Utpala.

00:15:18.851 --> 00:15:22.051
Blue Lotus is saying,
"Guess who that was?"

00:15:22.051 --> 00:15:23.579
KHO MO YIN

00:15:23.579 --> 00:15:25.078
What's that mean?

00:15:25.078 --> 00:15:26.040
KHO MO YIN

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.890
It's me. It was me.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:29.766
YIN TE

00:15:29.766 --> 00:15:33.950
DE DAG THAMS CAD LUS
KYIS MYONG BAR GYUR TO

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:38.937
And then I underwent all of
those sufferings in this body.

00:15:40.936 --> 00:15:42.742
DGE SLONG MA DE DAG GIS SMRAS PA

00:15:42.742 --> 00:15:45.491
The assembled nuns said to her,

00:15:45.491 --> 00:15:47.760
BSOD NAMS CI ZHIG BYAS NA,
SANGS RGYAS MTHONG ZHING

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.610
SANGS RGYAS KYIS BSU NAS RAB TU BYING STE

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.260
'KHOR BA'I MTHAR PHYIN PAR GYUR

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:56.460
They said, "But now tell
us the karma that you did

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:59.020
to lay eyes on the Buddha,

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.213
and to have the Buddha stand up

00:16:01.213 --> 00:16:03.470
and greet you and ask you to come to him,

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:07.820
And then for the Buddha to
arrange that you are ordained.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:08.978
And then to reach

00:16:08.978 --> 00:16:09.811
'KHOR BA'I MTHA'

00:16:09.811 --> 00:16:11.310
to go to the

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.540
'KHOR BA'I MTHA'

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.721
Yes, to reach the end
of the cycle of pain.

00:16:18.071 --> 00:16:21.215
Can you tell us the good story

00:16:21.215 --> 00:16:24.320
of why later in your
life you met the Buddha,

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:26.573
and you got ordained,
and you became an arhat?

00:16:26.573 --> 00:16:29.357
What happened there? She said,

00:16:29.357 --> 00:16:31.323
AUTPA LAS SMRAS PA

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:32.206
Utpala said,

00:16:32.206 --> 00:16:34.156
SNGON W'A RA n'A SI 'DIR

00:16:34.156 --> 00:16:36.714
"In a former life, here in Varanasi,"

00:16:36.714 --> 00:16:39.540
And Varanasi if you go there,
I mean, it's 5,000 years old.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:41.400
You can feel it.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.660
The people who live in Varanasi swear

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.190
it's a separate universe.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:48.150
They say it's not part of this world.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.440
And you can,

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.940
so many strange things happen in Varanasi.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:52.773
So anyway,

00:16:52.773 --> 00:16:54.830
W'A RA n'A SI 'DIR RI DRANG SRONG LHAGS

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:58.830
there was a place called
the place of the saints.

00:16:59.923 --> 00:17:00.756
RANG SANGS RGYAS

00:17:00.756 --> 00:17:02.256
There were RANG SANGS RGYASs

00:17:02.256 --> 00:17:04.820
NYAN THOSs and MU STEGS CAN.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:07.830
There were lots of saints living there.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:12.450
They were self-made
Buddhas, and listeners,

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:17.450
and non-Buddhists who possessed
the 5 kinds of clairvoyance.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:21.660
Which if you struggled
through Ben Kramer's text,

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.381
you know what they are.

00:17:24.381 --> 00:17:27.747
DE'I TSE NA RANG SANGS
RGYAS DAG CIG BSOD SNYOMS LA

00:17:27.747 --> 00:17:30.455
GRONG DU GSEGS PA DANG

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:32.330
Then there was...

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.065
I don't know if the
spelling here is wrong,

00:17:34.065 --> 00:17:37.410
but it seems to be a
pair of self-made Buddhas

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:40.944
went to the town, to the city,

00:17:40.944 --> 00:17:44.151
to beg for food.

00:17:44.151 --> 00:17:46.835
KHYIM BDAG CI CHUNG MA ZHIG GIS MTHONG NAS

00:17:46.835 --> 00:17:51.835
The wife of a certain family,

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.553
of a certain householder.

00:17:54.553 --> 00:17:56.120
RAB TU DGA'

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.570
By the way, RAB TU DGA'

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:01.840
is the name of the
first bodhisattva level.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:04.720
It's called Extreme Joy or something.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.610
She got extreme joy.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:08.560
By the way, maybe it's meaningful here,

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.222
that the same word, I don't know.

00:18:11.222 --> 00:18:12.732
BSOD SNYOMS PHUL NAS

00:18:12.732 --> 00:18:17.172
She gladly offered a meal to the monks,

00:18:17.172 --> 00:18:18.330
MCHOD PA BYAS SO

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.793
and made offerings to them.

00:18:19.793 --> 00:18:22.976
DE NAS RANG SANGS RGYAS
DE NAM MKHA' LA 'PHAGS TE

00:18:22.976 --> 00:18:25.034
Here's the word PHAGS PA.

00:18:25.034 --> 00:18:27.878
By the way, these ancient,
ancient sutras are so useful.

00:18:27.878 --> 00:18:32.680
So here's the word PHAGS PA
which usually means arya.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:35.140
Here it means to rise up.

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:39.621
So that self-made Buddha was,
"Mmm. That's a good meal,"

00:18:39.621 --> 00:18:42.748
and he rose up in the sky,

00:18:42.748 --> 00:18:43.931
LUS LA ME 'BAR

00:18:43.931 --> 00:18:46.763
and fire came out his body. Then,

00:18:46.763 --> 00:18:48.182
CHU 'BAB

00:18:48.182 --> 00:18:51.630
he dropped rain on Varanasi
to make everybody happy.

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.738
If you've ever been in
Varanasi in the summer,

00:18:54.738 --> 00:18:58.280
it's 44 or 45. People die
walking down the street.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.200
It's so hot. Then,

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:03.172
'GRO BA DANG, NYAL BA
DANG, 'DUG PA'I RDZU 'PHRUL

00:19:03.172 --> 00:19:06.550
he showed various miracles

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:11.225
in which he was either walking,
or laying down, or sitting.

00:19:11.225 --> 00:19:15.360
These are the traditional

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.720
modes of going through the day.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.861
Either you're sitting down,

00:19:19.861 --> 00:19:21.750
or you're walking, or laying down.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.816
And he went through,

00:19:23.816 --> 00:19:26.208
it means he went through the
whole day showing miracles.

00:19:26.208 --> 00:19:28.971
BSTAN NAS KHYIM BDAG GI CHUNG MA DES

00:19:28.971 --> 00:19:33.246
That housewife, she said,

00:19:33.246 --> 00:19:34.812
KHO MO YANG MA'ONGS PA'I DUS SU

00:19:34.812 --> 00:19:36.254
'DI 'DRA BA THOB BAR GYUR CIG

00:19:36.254 --> 00:19:38.700
"May I also in the
future become like him."

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:39.960
That's cool.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:42.130
That's so cool that he's flying in the sky

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:44.367
and he's shooting off fire,

00:19:44.367 --> 00:19:47.070
and he can rain on the whole city.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.833
I want to be like him in my future life.

00:19:49.833 --> 00:19:51.391
SMON LAM BTAB BO

00:19:51.391 --> 00:19:53.828
I made that prayer.

00:19:53.828 --> 00:19:58.219
DE'I TSE NA SMON LAM BTAB PA'I
KHYIM BDAG GI CHUNG MA DE NI

00:19:58.219 --> 00:20:01.520
The housewife who made the prayer

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.953
in those ancient times in Varanasi

00:20:03.953 --> 00:20:05.029
KHO MO YIN

00:20:05.029 --> 00:20:06.537
What's that mean, you guys?

00:20:06.537 --> 00:20:07.650
KHO MO YIN

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:10.490
That was me. That was me.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:13.000
Therefore, what's she going to say?

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.533
What is it?

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:19.391
The translation of
expecting something to come?

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.740
What's she going to say next?

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:26.740
That's why I saw the Buddha.
That's why he greeted me.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:30.740
That's why he got me ordained.
That's why I became an arhat.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:33.840
Let's check. Anticipatory translation.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.590
DE'I PHYIR DE BZHIN GSHEGS PA

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:36.806
That's why,

00:20:36.806 --> 00:20:40.200
PHRAD means that's why I met the Buddha.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:41.299
And that's why,

00:20:41.299 --> 00:20:42.550
SEMS RNAM PAR GROL

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.150
that's why my mind was liberated.

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.625
And I became a DGRA BCOM PA

00:20:46.625 --> 00:20:49.846
I became an arhat.

00:20:49.846 --> 00:20:54.371
'DI LTAR DGRA BCOM PA THOB MOD KYI

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.043
This a very moving sentence.

00:20:59.043 --> 00:21:00.859
She says, "Yes."

00:21:00.859 --> 00:21:03.670
MOD means "Yes, okay.
So I did achieve arhat,

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:07.400
but before that I went through a life,

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:11.180
which was like somebody holding a red hot

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:16.180
burning iron tongs at
my feet, to my feet."

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:21.440
It's like someone was holding
red hot iron to my feet

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.710
for the whole life before that.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.720
She says, "Yes, I got to arhat.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.330
It was cool, but don't forget before that

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:32.400
my whole life was like
someone was burning me

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.883
with a big red, hot piece of iron."

00:21:37.333 --> 00:21:41.356
RKANG MTHIL means to the soles of my feet.

00:21:41.356 --> 00:21:42.189
We had

00:21:42.189 --> 00:21:43.022
MTHIL DU

00:21:43.022 --> 00:21:44.463
THUGS DAM MTHIL DU BYUNG

00:21:44.463 --> 00:21:46.945
To hold the practice in your MTHIL.

00:21:46.945 --> 00:21:49.486
DE'I TSE RIGS CHE ZHING MTHO BA'I

00:21:49.486 --> 00:21:52.520
DGE SLONG MA LNGA BRGYA SNYED KYIS

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:56.530
Then these 500 nuns who
were listening to her story

00:21:56.530 --> 00:22:00.890
who happened to be of very high cast

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:02.930
before they became nuns,

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:07.190
SMRAS PA THOS NAS

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:10.885
having heard what she taught,

00:22:10.885 --> 00:22:15.885
LUS DANG SEMS SKYI G-YA' STE
'DONG BA LA ME MA MUR GYI

00:22:16.618 --> 00:22:20.010
PHUNG PO LTAR RTOGS NAS 'DOD
CHAGS KYI SEMS YONGS SU ZAD DE

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:22.151
Their 'DOD CHAGSs ZAD

00:22:22.151 --> 00:22:24.242
ZAD Z-A-D.

00:22:26.779 --> 00:22:30.820
This means disappearing.

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:33.820
Usually they use it for shoes.

00:22:33.820 --> 00:22:38.820
You know, automobile tires,
the rubber wears off,

00:22:39.108 --> 00:22:42.623
wears away. Their desires
suddenly disappeared.

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:48.550
Their desire to have a regular
home life just disappeared.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:53.782
They started to see the
home life like a DONG.

00:22:54.749 --> 00:22:59.416
DONG means a barbecue
pit for a cow, "vaca."

00:23:02.183 --> 00:23:07.180
ME MA MUR means glowing red embers.

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:11.350
So they started to see the home life

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:14.230
like a fire pit of glowing embers.

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:16.670
Not somewhere you'd want to be.

00:23:17.845 --> 00:23:20.186
KHYIM GYI SDUG BSNGAL
LA BTZON RA BAS KYANG

00:23:20.186 --> 00:23:22.078
LHAG PAR RTOGS TE

00:23:22.078 --> 00:23:25.180
BTZON RA BA means a prison.

00:23:25.180 --> 00:23:28.780
This instrumental is the comparative.

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:32.563
And this LHAG PA is
the LHAG in LHAG MTHONG

00:23:32.563 --> 00:23:34.260
which means vipashyana,

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:37.580
Which means super, super vision.

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:40.905
So they started to see that the KHYIM

00:23:40.905 --> 00:23:45.472
was LHAG than the BTZON RA.

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:51.460
The household life was worse

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:54.543
than being in prison your whole life.

00:23:56.335 --> 00:23:57.168
LHAG RTOGS

00:23:57.168 --> 00:24:01.630
RTOGS with an s. They suddenly woke up.

00:24:01.630 --> 00:24:04.343
They like, oh my god. They understood.

00:24:04.343 --> 00:24:06.600
DRI MA KUN ZAD NAS

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:11.050
Suddenly all their
imperfections, 'mala', right,

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:13.090
got vimala.

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:16.010
All their malas got vimala.

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:20.470
They went into TING NGE 'DZIN

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:23.470
and then DGRA BCOM PAR GYUR.

00:24:23.470 --> 00:24:24.812
They all became arhats.

00:24:24.812 --> 00:24:29.460
The 500 ladies all became arhat
just sitting there with her.

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:32.593
That seems pretty easy to me.

00:24:32.593 --> 00:24:34.809
DGE SLONG MA DE DAG GIS TSIG MTHUN PAR

00:24:34.809 --> 00:24:36.703
DGE SLONG MA AUTPAL LA BDAG CAG NI

00:24:36.703 --> 00:24:39.850
TSIG MTHUN PAR means in one voice.

00:24:39.850 --> 00:24:44.516
They said, the 500 new arhatesses

00:24:44.516 --> 00:24:47.541
said to the nun,

00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:50.554
Blue Lotus, Utpala,

00:24:50.554 --> 00:24:53.880
'DOD CHAGS KYIS KUN NAS
BCINGS SHING GLAGS PA LAS

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:57.110
We were...

00:24:57.110 --> 00:24:59.910
What's that song? Amazing Grace?

00:24:59.910 --> 00:25:04.910
We were chained in our
attachment to the home life,

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:09.734
but you broke the chains and
you taught us to be free.

00:25:09.734 --> 00:25:12.647
CHOS BSTAN PAS 'KHOR
BA'I MTHAR PHYIN PAR GYUR

00:25:12.647 --> 00:25:14.690
Because you taught us the Dharma,

00:25:14.690 --> 00:25:17.773
we have been MTHAR PHYIN.

00:25:17.773 --> 00:25:20.347
My Lama's name is MTHAR PHYIN.

00:25:20.347 --> 00:25:25.293
We have escaped the suffering of sansara.

00:25:27.013 --> 00:25:28.395
DE NAS BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS

00:25:28.395 --> 00:25:32.030
If you know sutras well,

00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:35.411
you can tell, you could smell
that we're coming to the end,

00:25:35.411 --> 00:25:38.227
because then the Buddha
gets up and says something.

00:25:38.227 --> 00:25:39.060
DE NAS BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS

00:25:39.060 --> 00:25:41.195
Then the Buddha stood up.

00:25:41.195 --> 00:25:43.970
DGE SLONG MA AUTPA LAS NI

00:25:43.970 --> 00:25:47.789
This teaching by the nun, Utpala

00:25:47.789 --> 00:25:52.370
LEGS PAR BSTAN LEGS SO LEGS SO

00:25:52.370 --> 00:25:54.637
That's awesome.

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:57.280
I can feel like the Dalai Lama

00:25:57.280 --> 00:26:00.348
standing up and saying, "That's awesome,

00:26:00.348 --> 00:26:01.391
that's a good teaching."

00:26:01.391 --> 00:26:03.741
BSTAN TO, GANG CHOS STON PA NI

00:26:03.741 --> 00:26:07.170
GCIG GIS GCIG BSTAN TE 'BRAS BU THOB NA

00:26:07.170 --> 00:26:12.170
When I see my students
teaching each other,

00:26:12.350 --> 00:26:17.070
and somebody gets to
a high spiritual level

00:26:17.070 --> 00:26:21.010
because they were sitting
together and teaching each other,

00:26:21.010 --> 00:26:23.180
it makes me so happy.

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:26.873
Then I think you are a real
daughter of the Buddha.

00:26:27.763 --> 00:26:30.413
Then it makes me feel like
you are a real daughter

00:26:30.413 --> 00:26:31.540
of the Buddha.

00:26:31.540 --> 00:26:35.520
If I see my daughters
making each other arhats,

00:26:35.520 --> 00:26:38.603
it makes dad so happy.

00:26:38.603 --> 00:26:39.860
ZHES BSNGAGS SO

00:26:39.860 --> 00:26:41.600
This BSNGAGS doesn't mean tantra,

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:44.790
it means he praised them.

00:26:44.790 --> 00:26:48.040
He said, "Wow, you guys are so cool."

00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:50.006
DE SKAD CES GSUNGS PA
LA 'KHOR MANG PO RJES SU

00:26:50.006 --> 00:26:51.874
YI RANG NAS MNGON PAR DGA'O

00:26:51.874 --> 00:26:55.520
When he had said that,
everybody was happy.

00:26:55.520 --> 00:26:57.840
That's the 25th...

00:26:57.840 --> 00:27:01.049
Thhus concludes the 25th chapter

00:27:01.049 --> 00:27:04.220
of the Sutra on the Wise and the Foolish

00:27:04.220 --> 00:27:08.930
named, The Chapter of the Nun Utpala.

00:27:08.930 --> 00:27:11.310
Yay! We're done.

00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:13.611
See you next class.

00:27:13.611 --> 00:27:15.540
Oh, don't forget why we had this.

00:27:15.540 --> 00:27:19.530
Why is this story coming here?

00:27:19.530 --> 00:27:20.860
Because Buddha is trying to say,

00:27:20.860 --> 00:27:24.618
you can't always see

00:27:24.618 --> 00:27:27.670
the relationships that
you had in the past.

00:27:27.670 --> 00:27:31.820
Like you could go through your whole life,

00:27:31.820 --> 00:27:33.970
unless you become an arhat,

00:27:33.970 --> 00:27:37.210
you won't understand why
all the troubles are coming

00:27:37.210 --> 00:27:38.320
to you in your life.

00:27:38.320 --> 00:27:41.630
And especially you won't
recognize who's been your mom

00:27:41.630 --> 00:27:43.280
before.

00:27:43.280 --> 00:27:45.596
Cool. Yay!

